+# INT8 low-rank projections without a repack
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+#
+# The checkpoint quantizes input_mix_weight_down / _up to INT8, group 64,
+# symmetric (compressed-tensors pack-quantized). Marlin and Humming both run
+# these shapes far below the memory bandwidth at decode batch sizes: the down
+# projection (320 x 10240) streams 3.3 MB in ~19 us, ~170 GB/s. Each decoder
+# layer runs two GatedResidual modules, and each one also launches a BF16
+# injection GEMV, the silu and the gate mix as separate kernels, ~32 us per
+# module at one token.
+#
+# The pack-quantized INT8 layout is already plain bytes: the int32 words hold
+# four values, least significant byte first, so weight_packed viewed as uint8
+# is q[N, K] with q = value + 128. The kernels below read that view directly,
+# so the weights stay exactly as loaded and cost no extra memory:
+#
+#   _hc_down_inject_silu_kernel  down (INT8) + injection (BF16) GEMV over the
+#                                normalized state, silu fused into the store
+#   _hc_up_gate_mix_kernel       up (INT8) GEMV with the gate mix over the HC
+#                                streams fused into the store
+#
+# Both round to BF16 at the same points as the unfused path. They take up to
+# _HC_FUSED_MAX_TOKENS tokens (the decode CUDA graph sizes); larger batches go
+# through _w8a16_gemm_kernel and the original silu / gate-mix kernels.
+# VLLM_HC_FUSED_INT8=0 keeps the original Marlin path.
